    "answer": "For location-change approvals related to remote work, employees must receive manager approval before changing their regular work location. Temporary changes within the same country for fewer than 15 business days may be approved by the manager, while longer changes require People Operations review. For cross-border or international remote work, People Operations review is required before travel, and such requests are considered ambiguous until tax, employment, and security implications are reviewed. The company does not maintain a formal visa or immigration policy in the employee knowledge base, and no specific visa application form is mentioned in the provided documents.",
